From 99838450043d252de86749a3082c6a9db6672894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:47:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] [TSReader] Read the last frames of a segment and of the
 stream

The demuxer emits a PES only when the next PES starts, and the H.264, HEVC
and MPEG-2 parsers emit a frame only when the next frame starts. So the last
frames of a segment came only after a read of the next segment.

A seek scan that read into the next segment could not seek back, because
AdaptiveStream seeks only in the current segment. A seek to the last frames
of a segment then continued at a later key frame. The scan now stops at the
end of the segment, reads the frames left in the buffers with the new
GetEndPacket(), and goes to the next segment only for a seek time after the
frames of the segment.

At the end of the stream, the reader also reads the frames left in the
buffers, so the last video frames and the audio of the last PES play. While
a live stream waits for the next segment, the frames stay in the buffers,
because a segment can end inside a PES.

A preceeding seek took a key frame after the seek time when the seek time
was between two frames, and CTSSampleReader::Seek rounded the seek time down
to one tick before the PTS of the frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
